course: dictionary
lesson: 4264
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around it, shows you which meaning the writer wants. The most common meaning of gravel is lots of small stones and bits of rock. «The children crunched across the gravel path.» The word crunch and the word path tell you the stones are under their feet.
explain: Gravel can also describe a voice. «Grandad's gravelly voice was low and rough.» There are no stones in his mouth! Here gravelly means low and rough-sounding. Ask yourself: does the meaning fit the sentence? Stones on a path makes sense for a path, but not for a voice.
explain: Gravel is also a useful science word. Water and weather break rocks into small bits, and those bits are gravel. Because water can drain through gravel, it is used under paths and in fish tanks. Always check which meaning fits before you decide.
fact: Gravel means lots of small stones and bits of rock.
fact: «Gravelly» can describe a voice that sounds low and rough.
fact: Gravel is made when water and weather break rocks into small bits.
fact: Gravel lets water drain through, so it is used under paths and in fish tanks.
fact: Loose gravel is slippery, so bikes can skid on it.
exercise: «Small wheels catch on gravel, and wrist guards and helmets protect against the falls.» What is gravel in this sentence? | A soft carpet of moss | A cake made with oats | *Lots of small stones and bits of rock | A kind of sticky mud
exercise: A singer has a gravelly voice. What does gravelly mean? | *Low and rough-sounding | Very quick and high | Soft as a whisper | Full of stones and very heavy
exercise: Find and copy the phrase from «At a school fair an older boy sold Mia «magic wishing stones» — gravel from the car park — for a pound each.» that tells you the stones were ordinary. | magic wishing stones | a pound each | at a school fair | *gravel from the car park
test: «Food gained by fraud tastes sweet, but one ends up with a mouth full of gravel.» What does gravel suggest here? | Something made of wood | *Something nasty and unpleasant | Something sweet to eat | Something very hot
test: Why is gravel used under paths and in fish tanks? | It stops rain from falling | It makes water boil faster | It only grows in water | *It lets water drain through
exam: Which is the best safety tip about gravel? | *Slow down and take care, because bikes can skid on loose gravel | Take off your helmet when you ride on gravel paths | Ride faster on gravel to keep your balance | Gravel is safe, so skid on it for fun
